# oracle: pair_style hybrid/overlay drip rebo - the examples' graphene/hydrogen data (data.CH: 545 atoms of C and H, boundary p p s; drip maps the C type and NULL for H), 10 NVE steps from 300 K instead of the example's minimization; compute pair c_0 (drip) and c_1 (rebo)
# measured (engine vs native, black box; rel over |value| >= 1e-6; per-atom scale max(1,|value|)): thermo max abs 6.7e-6 (press), max rel 3.7e-11; per-atom max scaled 1.4e-8 after 10 steps (1.6e-9 at step 0). The drip part is exact (c_0 at step 0: abs 1.1e-14); the rest is the REBO part (c_1 at step 0: abs 5.7e-10). Re-measured under Node 20 (black box, rolldown bundle of src/engine/interpreter): the same numbers, so the difference is not a Math-library rounding difference; it is in the existing REBO CH path, which this case uses unchanged
# oracle-inputs: w102il_drip_ch.data
# oracle-potentials: C.drip CH.rebo
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           metal
atom_style      molecular
boundary        p p s
read_data       w102il_drip_ch.data
pair_style      hybrid/overlay drip rebo
pair_coeff      * * drip C.drip C NULL
pair_coeff      * * rebo CH.rebo C H
compute         0 all pair drip
compute         1 all pair rebo
thermo_style    custom step pe etotal press c_0 c_1
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             0
velocity        all create 300.0 12345 dist gaussian mom yes rot yes
fix             1 all nve
timestep        1e-3
run             10
